# Security rules

- Never commit or log passwords, JWTs, Jira credentials, API keys, or private employee data.
- Replace Docker Compose defaults in production; defaults are local-development conveniences only.
- Validate and authorize every protected operation server-side.
- Use parameterized ORM queries and Pydantic boundary validation.
- Restrict production CORS to explicit origins.
- Validate upload MIME, size, extension, and destination; do not expose arbitrary filesystem paths.
- Keep tokens out of URLs except the existing WebSocket handshake until it can be replaced safely.
- Do not expose server-only environment variables through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Return safe error messages without stack traces or internal paths.
